showLastRefresh() in shop/js/script.js: your version (-) and the proposed one (+)

What changes:
1. The loop that removed aria-pressed from every day tab on each refresh is gone. That loop,
   plus pressing Monday again at the end, is why the tab jumped back to Monday after
   "Aktualizovat menu" while the table stayed on the chosen day.
2. Today is compared by the full date (toDateString), not only the day of the month
   (getDate: 3 October would match 3 November).
3. The "today" mark (aria-current="date") goes on the button (.day) and on the day title in
   the table (th), where styles.css looks for it, not on the <time> inside.
   It is also removed from the other days, so "dnes" no longer sticks to Monday.
4. A day is chosen only when no tab is pressed yet (the first time): today, or Monday if
   today is not in the week. The tab and data-day on .board are set together, so the tab and
   the table always show the same day.

Apply it:  git apply showLastRefresh.diff     (then delete this file)

